{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1178","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1178","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1178\",\"parent_revision\":\"1978dddd680e6440d0d647db8519379413e56fc6c7427d68b8c0fdbe9fa994fb\",\"root_revision\":\"1978dddd680e6440d0d647db8519379413e56fc6c7427d68b8c0fdbe9fa994fb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`github_project_setup.py` now has `milestone start` which bulk-transitions `status:needs-grooming` \u2192 `status:in-progress`. Add a symmetric `milestone close` command for the `complete-milestone` skill. The command should: (1) validate the milestone is open, (2) list all still-open issues (warn if any remain), (3) transition open issues from `status:in-progress` \u2192 `status:done` or close them, (4) close the milestone itself via `milestone.edit(state='closed')`, (5) print a completion summary. Updat\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **github_project_setup.py: add `milestone close` command** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #149 follow-up \u2014 start-milestone automation (2026-02-22)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-11)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Add a `milestone close` command to `github_project_setup.py` that symmetrically mirrors `milestone start`, for use by the `complete-milestone` skill.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- `github_project_setup.py milestone close --repo OWNER/REPO --number N [--dry-run]` is available and functional.\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n1. `milestone start` exists as the symmetric anchor | Requires: confirmed implementation | Why: close mirrors start semantics\\n2. `milestone close` command does not already exist | Requires: code inspection | Why: adding a duplicate would conflict\\n3. `complete-milestone` skill references `milestone close` | Requires: skill file inspection | Why: the skill is the consumer of this command\\n4. PyGithub `milestone.edit(state='closed')` API is available | Requires: confirmed in existing code | Why: closing milestone requires this call\\n5. Label transition logic (`status:in-progress` \u2192 `status:done`) is implementable | Requires: existing label utilities | Why: core behavior of the command\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `milestone start` exists: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `github_project_setup.py` line 194 `@milestone_app.command('start')`\\n- `milestone close` does NOT already exist: MISSING \u2014 command IS already implemented | Evidence: `github_project_setup.py` lines 259-319, `@milestone_app.command('close')` with full implementation\\n- `complete-milestone` skill references `milestone close`: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `.claude/skills/complete-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 107-118 already call `github_project_setup.py milestone close --number {number}`\\n- `milestone.edit(state='closed')` API: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `github_project_setup.py` line 304 `milestone.edit(title=milestone.title, state='closed')`\\n- Label transition utilities: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `_transition_to_done()` function at line 322, `_ensure_label()` used at line 300\\n\\nDecision:\\n- BLOCKED on original premise \u2014 the requested feature already exists in full.\\n\\nFinding:\\nThe `milestone close` command described in this item is fully implemented as of the current codebase. All five requirements from the item description are satisfied:\\n1. Validates milestone is open via `_get_open_milestone()` (raises if closed)\\n2. Lists all still-open issues with labels before acting (lines 276-288)\\n3. Transitions open issues from `status:in-progress` \u2192 `status:done` via `_transition_to_done()` (lines 299-301)\\n4. Closes the milestone via `milestone.edit(title=milestone.title, state='closed')` (line 304)\\n5. Prints completion summary including counts (lines 305-316)\\n\\nAdditionally, the `complete-milestone` skill already references the command in Step 4 of its workflow.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen run against an open milestone:\\n- Prints a count of open and closed issues in the milestone\\n- Lists each open issue with its current labels\\n- Transitions all open issues: removes `status:in-progress` or `status:needs-grooming` labels, adds `status:done`\\n- Closes the milestone via the GitHub API\\n- Prints a summary: how many issues were transitioned, skipped (already done), or failed\\n- With `--dry-run`: prints what would happen without making changes\\n- With `--project-number`: also updates Projects V2 Status to `Done` for all milestone issues\\n- Exits non-zero if any label update fails\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe command `github_project_setup.py milestone close --repo OWNER/REPO --number N [--dry-run] [--project-number N] [--owner OWNER]` is registered under `milestone_app` as a Typer subcommand and callable from the `complete-milestone` skill workflow.\\n\\nThis structure is already in place: the command is registered at line 259, the skill references it at `.claude/skills/complete-milestone/SKILL.md` Step 4.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run .claude/skills/gh/scripts/github_project_setup.py milestone close --help` exits 0 and prints the command signature including `--number`, `--repo`, `--dry-run`, `--project-number`, `--owner` options.\\n2. Running against an open milestone with open issues: all open issues receive `status:done` label, `status:in-progress` label is removed, and the milestone state becomes `closed`.\\n3. Running with `--dry-run`: no labels are changed, milestone remains open, output shows what would change.\\n4. Running against an already-closed milestone: command exits with an error (non-zero) without making changes.\\n5. Running with `--project-number`: Projects V2 Status is updated to `Done` for all milestone issues.\\n6. Exit code is non-zero when any individual label update fails.\\n7. The `complete-milestone` skill Step 4 invocation `uv run .claude/skills/gh/scripts/github_project_setup.py milestone close --number {number}` succeeds without modification.\\n\\nNOTE: Based on codebase inspection, criteria 1, 3, 4, 6, and 7 are already satisfied. Criteria 2 and 5 require a live milestone test to fully verify.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/gh/scripts/github_project_setup.py` (lines 259-358: `milestone_close` implementation) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/complete-milestone/SKILL.md` (lines 102-118: Step 4 references `milestone close`) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/gh/scripts/github_project_setup.py` (lines 194-256: `milestone_start` for comparison) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\nRelated (not blocking): `complete-milestone` skill (#849 \u2014 update peripheral skill references) uses this command in its Step 4 workflow.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- IMPLEMENTATION ALREADY EXISTS: The `milestone close` command is fully implemented in `github_project_setup.py` at lines 259-319. This item should be verified against the live GitHub API (requires a real milestone) and then closed as done, or reassigned to track missing test coverage if desired.\\n- No unresolved blockers if the goal is verification-and-close.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 verification only. The implementation is complete. A live API smoke-test against a real milestone is the only remaining work to confirm acceptance criteria 2 and 5. Candidate for immediate resolution.\\n\",\"digest\":\"2afd4e490a13d53c22b2ba2544780fda8b5bfc705dd8233d8fc68270803da084\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVV-NFg\"}"}